WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.567
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:05.901
You're here. You're watching it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.968
Thank you very much.

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:09.667
Well, guys, earlier tonight,

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:13.000
President Biden delivered
the State of the Union address.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.334
Yep. Of course, Democrats
spent most of the night

00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:16.767
clapping for Biden.

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:17.868
It wasn't for anything he said.

00:00:17.868 --> 00:00:19.033
They were just trying to
keep him awake.

00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:23.367
They were like, "Alright, hey...
Hey! Come on."

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:26.634
It was a tough night
for all of Biden's staffers

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:27.767
watching from The White House,

00:00:27.767 --> 00:00:28.834
'cause every time
people clapped,

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:30.868
the lights went on and off.

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:35.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:38.534
♪♪

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.033
It's the same thing every year.
One side stands and claps.

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:43.467
The other side sits still,
not having any fun.

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:44.934
It reminds me
of my cousin's wedding.

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:47.534
Yeah. "I give it six months!"

00:00:47.534 --> 00:00:50.734
Now, Biden also talked about
his achievements.

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:52.534
He said, "We passed an
infrastructure bill,

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:53.701
we reduced inflation,

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:55.934
and we finally convinced
Tom Brady to retire."

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:57.601
So I think it's a great year.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:01:00.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:03.667
In his speech, Biden called
for bipartisanship and unity.

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.501
He was like,
"As Democrats and Republicans,

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:09.767
we have one common goal -- to
mishandle classified documents."

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:13.701
There was wall-to-wall coverage
of the State of the Union

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:17.601
on all the major networks,
like NBC, ABC, and CBS.

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:21.367
Meanwhile,
Netflix is like, "Ka-ching."

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:25.200
I read that Biden's approval
rating currently stands at 42%,

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.634
just above the 41% he had at
last year's State of the Union.

00:01:29.634 --> 00:01:30.801
That's tough.

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:32.267
It's like eating kale
for an entire year,

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:35.100
then realizing you only lost
1 pound, and you go,

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.000
"I did this for a whole year."

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.868
At the State of the Union,

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.234
Biden was excited to talk about
all of his accomplishments.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.667
I think he even wanted to mess
with China a little bit.

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:46.300
Take a look at
his entrance tonight.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:51.534
-Mr. Speaker, the
President of the United States!

00:01:51.534 --> 00:01:54.300
-♪ All I do is
win, win, win no matter what ♪

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.501
♪ Got money on my mind,
I can never get enough ♪

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:59.434
-That's how he entered.
That's how he entered.

00:01:59.434 --> 00:02:04.133
-Just rubbing it in their face.
My goodness.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:05.934
-That's an entrance right there.
-That is an entrance.

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:08.701
-Yeah. Well,
speaking of the balloon,

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:11.133
the U.S. Navy has
started to recover parts of

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:13.067
the Chinese balloon
that was shot down over

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:14.367
the Atlantic Ocean.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.968
Not only did we find
the balloon,

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.734
all the Navy divers
came back speaking

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:20.033
in that funny helium voice.

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:22.634
[ High-pitched ]
"Mission accomplished!"

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:23.834
[ Normal voice ]
Listen to this, guys.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.801
Today, Speaker Kevin McCarthy
suggested that

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:29.901
Congressman George Santos
will face a House investigation.

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:32.601
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:35.734
The specific charges
are "everything."

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:38.133
Some news from overseas.

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:40.801
I saw that Kim Jong-un
just reappeared in public

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:43.200
for the first time in 36 days.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.133
Tough news for North Korea --
when Kim Jong-un emerged,

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:50.100
he saw his shadow, which means
six more weeks of dictatorship.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:54.901
Thank you.

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.868
Yep, Kim Jong-un hadn't attended
any social functions

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:01.434
in over a month.

00:03:01.434 --> 00:03:05.334
So either something is wrong or
he was just doing Dry January.

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:08.968
Switching gears, Tom Brady
announced that, next year,

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:12.167
he will start his broadcasting
career at Fox Sports.

00:03:12.167 --> 00:03:14.667
But the statement from
Fox Sports seemed a bit off.

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:15.701
Here, check this out.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:43.267
-I didn't think
they'd release that.

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:45.434
-Huh?

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:46.701
-I didn't think
they'd release that.

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:48.300
You'd think they'd go,
"Oh, we made a mistake.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.667
We'll keep it back."
You know what I mean?

00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:51.100
But they let it out there.
That's great.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.701
-I think they just went with,
like, a live commercial

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:54.167
and they just didn't
have the time.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.400
You know, sometimes, you just
got to put that out there.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.000
-Keep on going, yeah.
-Breaking news.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.200
-Yeah, exactly.
Live commercials.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.901
Everybody loves them.
-Yeah, so fun.

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:02.367
Well, people are
talking about this.

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:05.300
Apparently, the "Yellowstone"
series starring Kevin Costner

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.501
is set to end.

00:04:06.501 --> 00:04:07.701
[ Audience groans ]

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:09.634
And a spin-off starring
Matthew McConaughey

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:10.834
could be in the works.

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:11.968
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:04:11.968 --> 00:04:13.300
Yeah, they already have
a title for it.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:15.734
It's going to be called
"Yellowstoned."

00:04:16.667 --> 00:04:18.567
Genius.

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:21.033
That's a good idea.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:23.601
I'd watch that.

00:04:23.601 --> 00:04:26.200
Did you guys hear about
a Kia recall?

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.934
It's not great.
Take a look at this.

00:04:27.934 --> 00:04:30.901
-A recall alert if you drive
a Kia S.U.V.

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:34.601
The company is recalling
the Telluride three-row S.U.V.

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:37.934
over faulty second-row
side airbags.

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:41.067
-Aw, man!
I just bought a Kia S.U.V.

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:42.868
-Oh, Geez. I'm sorry, Tariq.

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:44.200
-It's all good.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.067
I mean, at least I still have
my trusty Honda.

00:04:47.067 --> 00:04:50.000
It's an older vehicle,
but that's okay.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.901
-Oh.

00:04:51.901 --> 00:04:53.467
-"Oh" what?

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:55.067
-Roll the clip.

00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:57.167
-A recall alert
for you this morning.

00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:59.567
Honda is urging owners of around

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:02.834
8,000 older vehicles
to not drive them.

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:05.467
The airbag inflaters
have a high possibility of

00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:09.067
exploding and
hurling shrapnel in a crash.

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:12.033
-What?! How am I supposed to
get to my friend's

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:13.934
Super Bowl party this weekend?

00:05:13.934 --> 00:05:16.167
-I'm not sure.
I'm sorry about that, Tariq.

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:18.167
-I had it all planned out.

00:05:18.167 --> 00:05:20.701
I was going to bring
my charcuterie board.

00:05:20.701 --> 00:05:22.801
I bought
six different packages --

00:05:22.801 --> 00:05:25.200
excuse me, eight packages.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.634
Eight different packages of
ready-to-eat meats.

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:29.234
-A recall alert for you,

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:31.334
and it deals with
your charcuterie board.

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:34.100
Six different packages -- excuse
me, eight different packages

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:37.400
of ready-to-eat meat could be
contaminated with listeria.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.701
-Come on!

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:41.000
-It's a tough break.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.801
Is there anything else
that you can bring to the party?

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:45.467
-Well, thankfully,
I'm always prepared.

00:05:45.467 --> 00:05:47.868
In my kitchen right now,
I've got like

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:51.067
2.5 million pounds
of canned meat.

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:53.467
-There you go. That's perfect.
What time is the party?

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:54.934
-Well, kickoff is at 6:30,

00:05:54.934 --> 00:05:59.033
but I'll get there a little bit
early, around six-twenty-fooa --

00:05:59.033 --> 00:06:00.367
six-twenty-four.

00:06:00.367 --> 00:06:01.801
-Time right now,
it is six-twenty-fooa --

00:06:01.801 --> 00:06:02.868
six-twenty-four.

00:06:02.868 --> 00:06:04.534
A recall alert
for something that may be

00:06:04.534 --> 00:06:06.767
in your kitchen right now.

00:06:06.767 --> 00:06:08.367
Conagra is recalling more than

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:11.133
2.5 million pounds
of canned meat.

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:13.267
-Are you kidding me?!

00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:15.067
-Do you have anything else?

00:06:15.067 --> 00:06:17.200
-I'd have to check my pantries.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.300
Maybe my Rao's.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.801
I have some 16-ounce jars of

00:06:21.801 --> 00:06:23.968
made-for-home
slow-simmered soup.

00:06:23.968 --> 00:06:29.100
They're labeled
chicken and...gnocchi?

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:31.000
-We have a recall alert
new at 5:30.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.067
Check your pantries.

00:06:32.067 --> 00:06:35.767
Rao's is recalling
some 16-ounce jars

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:39.300
of made-for-home
slow-simmered soup.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:42.901
The affected jars are labeled
chicken and...gnocchi?

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.200
-Man, I give up!

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.267
-Why don't you come to my
Super Bowl party.

00:06:48.267 --> 00:06:51.534
-Sure. What do you have planned?

00:06:51.534 --> 00:06:53.434
-Well, you know
I live above Two Rivers Coffee,

00:06:53.434 --> 00:06:54.901
so we're going to do
a hot-cocoa party,

00:06:54.901 --> 00:06:57.300
because they have these cool
peanut-butter hot-chocolate pods

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.868
including Brooklyn
Peanut Butter Cup Hot Cocoa,

00:06:59.868 --> 00:07:03.334
Pingo...Peanut...Butter...
Cookie...Hot...Chocolate,

00:07:03.334 --> 00:07:06.000
and Cold Stone
Peanut Butter Cup Perfection.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.434
-Oh.

00:07:07.434 --> 00:07:09.534
-"Oh" what?

00:07:09.534 --> 00:07:11.601
-Roll the clip.

00:07:11.601 --> 00:07:13.400
-Two Rivers Coffee
is recalling its

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:15.334
peanut-butter
hot-chocolate pods,

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:18.701
including Brooklyn Bean
Peanut Butter Cup Hot Cocoa,

00:07:18.701 --> 00:07:21.300
Pingo...Peanut...Butter...
Cookie...Hot...Chocolate,

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:23.934
and Cold Stone
Peanut Butter Cup Perfection.

00:07:23.934 --> 00:07:25.267
-You know what? Forget it.

00:07:25.267 --> 00:07:27.200
Just come over,
and we'll rewatch the Grammys.

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:28.701
Tariq Trotter, everybody.
-Jimmy Fallon.

00:07:28.701 --> 00:07:30.434
-That is Tariq Trotter,
the one and only.

00:07:30.434 --> 00:07:32.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:32.601 --> 00:07:34.067
Thank you.

00:07:34.067 --> 00:07:35.100
Wow.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.934
Difficult to make plans.

00:07:37.934 --> 00:07:39.734
Finally, experts in California

00:07:39.734 --> 00:07:41.734
discovered a pretty crazy
issue at one house.

00:07:41.734 --> 00:07:42.901
Check this out.

00:07:42.901 --> 00:07:44.701
-A pest-control company
encountered a home

00:07:44.701 --> 00:07:46.834
that had been experiencing
damage from a woodpecker.

00:07:46.834 --> 00:07:48.100
And look at this.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.834
The bird had been storing acorns
in the home's walls.

00:07:51.834 --> 00:07:54.067
700 pounds of acorns.

00:07:54.067 --> 00:07:56.100
-Oof!

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:58.701
The woodpecker was like, "Well,
there goes my Super Bowl party.

00:07:58.701 --> 00:08:00.434
We have a great show.

00:08:00.434 --> 00:08:01.501
Give it up for The Roots,
ladies and gentlemen!

00:08:01.501 --> 00:08:02.567
-Let's go.
♪♪

00:08:02.567 --> 00:08:05.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
Uh-huh.

00:08:05.367 --> 00:08:06.567
Yeah.

00:08:06.567 --> 00:08:09.434
We goin' all
the way up with this one.

00:08:09.434 --> 00:08:11.634
"21 Pounds."

00:08:11.634 --> 00:08:13.634
Ha!

00:08:13.634 --> 00:08:15.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:15.367 --> 00:08:18.200
-Thank you very much, everyone.
Welcome.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.200
Before we start the show,
I just want to mention

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.234
UNICEF is on the ground
right now

00:08:23.234 --> 00:08:25.801
supporting our friends in
Syria and Turkey.

00:08:25.801 --> 00:08:26.934
They're providing access to

00:08:26.934 --> 00:08:29.033
clean water, food,
and much more.

00:08:29.033 --> 00:08:31.100
So if you're able to give,
please visit

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:34.567
unicefusa.org/tonightshow.

00:08:34.567 --> 00:08:36.934
Every little bit counts.
We appreciate that.

00:08:36.934 --> 00:08:38.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

